## 3. Longest Substring Without Repeating Characters

## Approach - Sliding Window + HashSet
--  Use two pointers: left and right.
--  Store characters of the current window in a HashSet.
--  Move right through the string.
--  If the character already exists, move left and remove characters until the duplicate is gone.
--  Add the current character to the set.
--  Update maxLen with right - left + 1.
--  Return maxLen.

## Complexity :
Time: O(n)
Space: O(k), k is number of unique characters

SOLUTION :
class Solution {
    public int lengthOfLongestSubstring(String s) {
        int left = 0;
        int maxLen = 0;
        HashSet<Character> set = new HashSet<>();
        for (int right = 0; right < s.length(); right++) {
            while (set.contains(s.charAt(right))) {
                set.remove(s.charAt(left));
                left++;
            }
            set.add(s.charAt(right));
            maxLen = Math.max(maxLen, right - left + 1);
        }
        return maxLen;
    }
}
